germany's foreign ministry is calling  for a transparent probe into abuse  claims after more evidence emerged of  china's brutal crackdown on its  predominantly muslim uighur minority a  cache of documents dubbed the xinjiang  police files was leaked to international  media including photographs inside  xinjiang's mass incarceration facilities  it's a rare look behind the walls of a  so-called re-education camp in the  northwestern chinese province the photos  show police using physical force against  prisoners in handcuffs and chains the  leak was published by a consortium of  investigative journalists including from  the bbc and to germany's der spiegel and  ard the publication coincides with the  arrival in china of the u.n human rights  commissioner michelle bachelet  we're now joined by frederick obama from  the german media outlet der spiegel he  is one of the about 30 investigative  journalists behind this story so very  good to have you with us  uh first of all after years of denial by  the chinese government your research  gives hundreds of thousands of abused  uighurs a face  please help us to understand the meaning  of it by sharing the story that stood  out most for you  i think  the most important thing about the  xinjiang police files is that we now see  faces attached to this crime against  humanity we see thousands of people  detained  in camps in northwestern china  we see 15 year old children being  detained up to  all the elderly uh women like 73 year  old woman being detained there and first  of all first and foremost we see the  argument of the chinese government  counted the argumentation so far was  that this is vocational schools that  people are there on their own will they  they could leave whenever they want but  in the documents that were leaked to us  we see now a shoot to kill policy we see  that the uyghurs in those camps were  held there by force  now the data set consists of uh more  than 5000 photos many of them showing  sensitive and security related footage  do we know who they take them and why  no we don't know who exactly um  uh took those photos we have hints that  it was people working in those camps  taking them  like for example mugshots of the people  detained there and then like making  photos of their exercises of them  treating  the detailed individuals  and then the data  was obtained by a source who leaked it  to a german  scientist called adrian sense  so far we have to  think that  the source could be a hacker  obviously the data comes from within the  chinese  government and authority operators and  we were able to independently verify uh  the documents and the photos  i mean it is a strange thought to think  that the handling of the people would be  documented in in such a way  do we know or how could you assess that  these pictures are actually real and not  fake  well first and foremost we  did hire independent experts who looked  and checked the authenticity of the  photos if they were manipulated in any  way  um then we at a second step we did  geolocate those many of those photos for  example whenever you could see something  uh in the uh pictures that was outside  of the camps for example walls towers  um and stuff like that and we were we  were able to geolocate them  with the help of satellite images we  also were able to  find uh information in the metadata of  the photos that showed us that they were  taken within um camps that could be seen  from space  via satellites  and then we also were able um to speak  with us living outside china  and who could um  let their relatives  that we have seen on those photos and  and on the list of uh detained  individuals that they were  disappeared basically several months or  even years ago okay  well thank you so much frederic  obermeyer from german media outlet der  spiegel one of the about 30  investigative journalists behind this  story thank you so much for sharing it  with us  thanks for having me
 

